<title>GERMANY: TABLE - WESTLB DETAILS H1 RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TABLE - WESTLB DETAILS H1 RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    749.6  vs 611.5</p>
<p>    Group risk provisions		     206.4  vs 260.0</p>
<p>    Group oper profit before provisions   956.0  vs 871.5</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 1,928  vs 1,814</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     374.3  vs 365.2</p>
<p>    Group net income from trading	   274.0  vs 228.8</p>
<p>    Group personnel expenses		  946.4  vs 903.5</p>
<p>    Group other administrative expenses   732.7  vs 750.2</p>
<p>    Group other operating income	    59.1   vs 116.9</p>
<p>    Group total assets			 520,379 vs 465,832</p>
<p>    Group business volume		    641,786 vs 579,225</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Westdeutsche Landesbank Girozentrale. The bank also said it expected a continued positive earnings trend in 1997. Results compare with six-twelfths of the full-year 1996 results -- a practice abandoned by many German banks which have switched to year-on-year comparisons but still pursued by some banks which believe it irons out fluctuations and gives a truer picture of a bank's performance.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
